12
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.460
And we're going to start first with our Snapshot.

13
00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:02.460
So I'm going to walk over here just to prove to you that we're not using any editing voodoo for this.

14
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.459
We're interactively changing this.

15
00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:08.489
And we're working in 5.1 for this particular feature.

16
00:01:08.489 --> 00:01:20.620
So I'm working with this iPad here, and you'll notice I have several different lighting scenarios loaded within my RCP.

17
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:28.620
And we have it connected right now directly inside of our web remote.

18
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:34.620
Now, you'll see, because we chose that Snapshot in the very beginning, which you saw me do on the menu,

19
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.620
it's now loaded all of my Snapshots, so it recognizes them.

20
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:43.620
You'll also notice that I have a Take Snapshot at the top, so you do have that option too.

21
00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:49.620
These are game changer concepts here, because before you could load your Snapshots and you could work with them,

22
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:55.620
but because Lumen wasn't quite there yet, it wasn't fully optimized, you'd have to pre-bake a few things,

23
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.620
and then your scene would have to be pretty bare bones if you're working with Lumen.

24
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.620
Lumen is optimized quite well here, and you'll see that we also have water moving in the background.

25
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.620
We have a decent scene.

26
00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.620
Now, again, everything within context, everything with a grain of salt,

27
00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:13.620
you can always put things to a complete halt if you put too many stuff in there.

28
00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.620
So just always think about optimization when you're working with things.

29
00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.620
But you'll notice we have our scenes loaded perfectly in here, which is great,

30
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.620
and I don't have to rebuild any lighting here because I'm using Lumen,

31
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.620
and I'm loading these on the fly, and I can have quite a bit if I needed,

32
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.620
because we've optimized Snapshot to work with Lumen to work and perform a lot better than it used to.

33
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.620
But do keep things in mind. Don't throw the whole kitchen sink at it at first.

34
00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.620
Walk yourself through each one of these levels if you load them,

35
00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.620
and just be conscious of where your stuff is at, how much items you have,

36
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.620
and exactly how complicated your lighting and your scenes are.

37
00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.620
But overall, this is fantastic, and it's a great new update for Unreal.

38
00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.620
So I'm going to go ahead and click on our first one here,

39
00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.620
