43
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.580
We're only working with three, and everything's working beautifully in our scene.

44
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.580
You see the shadows moving with the palm tree. Fantastic.

45
00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.610
And then we'll go to the next one here, evening.

46
00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:33.610
I'm going to hit Apply Snapshot, and then we've got a nice, more evening setting here.

47
00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.639
And awesome.

48
00:03:35.639 --> 00:03:39.639
We're able to do this on the fly, and you can now do this on set,

49
00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:42.639
working with your directors, working with your production managers,

50
00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:44.639
working with whoever's in charge of your light,

51
00:03:44.639 --> 00:03:47.639
whether it's big production or small production,

52
00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:50.639
you're able to access this via your iPad,

53
00:03:50.639 --> 00:03:54.639
and you're able to go in here and edit things according to what you need.

54
00:03:54.639 --> 00:03:59.990
Now let's go ahead and go to our tab one, which is our light control.

55
00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:04.990
So we're back at evening now, and now I can control my intensity of my light,

56
00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.990
so I can lower the intensity or increase the intensity.

57
00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:16.670
I can go in here and change the color of a light if I need to.

58
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.699
Ooh, that's really gross.

59
00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:26.139
So we'll reset back to default, and we'll say yes to default.

60
00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.459
And then we can also control the roll if we need to.

61
00:04:30.459 --> 00:04:42.139
We can control the pitch, move that around.

62
00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:48.500
Let's put that back. There we go.

63
